NNAAMMEE
     bbccee — QLogic NetXtreme II (BCM5706/5708/5709/5716) PCI/PCIe Gigabit Eth‐
     ernet adapter driver

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     To compile this driver into the kernel, place the following lines in your
     kernel configuration file:

           ddeevviiccee mmiiiibbuuss
           ddeevviiccee bbccee

     Alternatively, to load the driver as a module at boot time, place the
     following line in loader.conf(5):

           if_bce_load="YES"

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbccee driver supports QLogic's NetXtreme II product family, including
     the BCM5706, BCM5708, BCM5709 and BCM5716 Ethernet controllers.

     The NetXtreme II product family is composed of various Converged NIC (or
     CNIC) Ethernet controllers which support a TCP Offload Engine (TOE), Re‐
     mote DMA (RDMA), and iSCSI acceleration, in addition to standard L2 Eth‐
     ernet traffic, all on the same controller.

     The following features are supported in the bbccee driver under FreeBSD:

           IP/TCP/UDP checksum offload
           Jumbo frames (up to 9022 bytes)
           VLAN tag stripping
           Interrupt coalescing
           10/100/1000Mbps operation in full-duplex mode
           10/100Mbps operation in half-duplex mode

     The bbccee driver supports the following media types:

     aauuttoosseelleecctt   Enable autoselection of the media type and options.  The
                  user can manually override the autoselected mode by adding
                  media options to rc.conf(5).

     1100bbaasseeTT//UUTTPP  Set 10Mbps operation.  The ifconfig(8) mmeeddiiaaoopptt option can
